ional\n875:### 54. `p6-socs-09` — Safety and Security — Staying Safe as a Citizen\n891:### 55. `p6-socs-10` — Technology and Society\n907:### 56. `p6-socs-11` — Civic Role Models in Nigeria\n923:### 57. `p6-socs-12` — Population Growth and Civic Responsibility\n939:### 58. `p6-socs-13` — Entrepreneurship and Self-Reliance\n955:### 59. `p6-socs-14` — Peace Education and Conflict Prevention\n971:### 60. `p6-socs-15` — Revision and Consolidation — Bridge to JSS1\n# Style B — Social Studies P3–P6 — 60-image ChatGPT-pasteable prompt set\n\nGenerated directly from the approved image-design-intent manifests (`tools/image-manifest/p{3,4,5,6}-socs-image-manifest*.json`) using the Style B prompt template locked 2026-07-12 and confirmed working after the 3-image pilot test (2026-07-17, `tasks/2026-07-17-styleB-3image-qa-result.md`).\n\n**Workflow per image:**\n1. Copy the \"Prompt\" text into ChatGPT.\n2. Copy the \"Avoid\" text as a follow-up instruction (or append it to the prompt as \"Avoid: ...\").\n3. Download the result and save it under `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/` with the **exact filename** given (do not rename).\n4. Once a band (or all 60) is done, tell Claude — QA review, overlay compositing, and guarded promotion into `app/images/` happen after.\n\n**Recommended order:** one band at a time (P3 → P4 → P5 → P6), reviewing each band's results before starting the next — same discipline used for the content-authoring phase.\n\n---\n\n\n## Band P3 (15 images)\n\n### 1. `p3-socs-01` — The Meaning and Importance of Social and Citizenship Studies\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-01.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-01.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A Northern Nigerian primary-school courtyard where girls and boys work together: two pupils place litter in a bin, two care for shared books, and two calmly discuss a simple classroom matter with a teacher nearby, showing observation, cooperation, rules, and care for public property. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Show equal participation by girls and boys; no religious, ethnic, political-party, or status symbols; do not portray any child as naturally obedient, disruptive, or dominant because of gender or background.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Haɗin kai, Kayan jama’a\n\n---\n\n### 2. `p3-socs-02` — Our Local Government Area\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-02.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-02.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A simple, non-geographic community map connecting a neutral local government (LGA) office to a market, a water point, a school, a health centre, and a clean local road; small diverse groups of residents give information to an office worker and use the services. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Use no real seal, party colour, candidate portrait, campaign sign, named office-holder, or claim that one authority alone provides every service; depict women and men as residents and workers.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Ofishin Ƙaramar Hukuma, Kasuwa, Wurin ruwa, Makaranta, Cibiyar lafiya\n\n---\n\n### 3. `p3-socs-03` — Community Needs and Services\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-03.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-03.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A child-friendly community-needs map with paired need-and-service examples: clean water and a repaired pump, learning and a school, health and a health centre, safe passage and a drained road, plus pupils reporting a problem to an adult rather than repairing hazards themselves. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Children must only observe and report; do not show them entering drains, handling tools, repairing pumps, directing traffic, or doing hazardous sanitation work.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Ruwa mai tsabta, Hidimar jama’a, Magudanar ruwa, Cibiyar lafiya\n\n---\n\n### 4. `p3-socs-04` — Transportation — Road and Rail\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-04.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-04.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. Two side-by-side transport scenes: a calm paved road with a car, bicycle, and produce truck, and a passenger train moving on a fenced rail line; a separate safe-crossing inset shows a child with an adult stopping and looking both ways away from the tracks. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clea