d and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. No airline logo, national flag, military aircraft, overcrowding, rough water, standing passengers, unaccompanied child, or person without a life jacket; no one should be shown entering water.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Filin jirgin sama, Jirgin ruwa, Rigar kariya ta ruwa\n\n---\n\n### 6. `p3-socs-06` — Communication — Traditional Methods\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-06.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-06.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A respectful Northern Nigerian market-square scene showing a town announcer delivering a community message while a second adult uses a drum or kalangu; nearby women, men, and children listen calmly, with subtle sound lines indicating that the message reaches people nearby. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Avoid caricature, costume-as-spectacle, royal or political insignia, religious hierarchy, alarm or panic, and claims that one drum pattern has a universal meaning; depict the methods as locally agreed communication.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Mai shela, Ganga ko kalangu, Saƙo\n\n---\n\n### 7. `p3-socs-07` — Communication — Modern Methods\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-07.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-07.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. Four clear panels in a Northern Nigerian home-and-school setting: a family listening to radio news, pupils watching an educational television programme with a teacher, an adult making a telephone call, and a child using a mobile phone beside a trusted adult; a small signal icon shows that access varies by place. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Show supervised, purposeful device use; no brand logos, social-media interfaces, phone numbers, personal data, harmful messages, political broadcasts, or implication that every household has electricity, signal, or a device.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Rediyo, Talabijin, Waya, Wayar hannu, Bayanin sirri\n\n---\n\n### 8. `p3-socs-08` — Our Natural Environment\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-08.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-08.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A labeled Northern Nigerian natural landscape with broad land, grasses, scattered trees, low rocks, a modest river or pond, open air, birds, livestock, and wild animals at a safe distance; a small seasonal inset contrasts greener rainy-season vegetation with dry-season ground. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Use a realistic but non-alarming dryland landscape; do not depict drought victims, dead animals, disaster, ethnic costume markers, political boundaries, unsafe water collection, or a claim that all Northern Nigerian environments look identical.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
